; AN AXTAG ON THE FIRST DECLARATION A TEMPLATE GENERATES.
;
; `tests/diagnostics/361-macro-template-effect.ax` records three bugs
; that stood between an author and a claim written inside a macro
; template, and closed them. This is the fourth, and it was invisible
; to 361 because 361's tag sits on the template's FIFTH declaration.
;
; `expCopyDeclInto` copies the first generated declaration into the
; INVOCATION's node - the node that already sits in the top-level list -
; and it copied words 0,1,2,3,4,5,6 and 9 while writing a literal 0
; into word 7, the AXTAGs. So a tag on element 0 of a template was
; parsed, attached by `attachAxtags`, copied by `expBuildDecls`, and
; then thrown away. Measured before the fix, with one near-miss key
; moved one line between two runs of the same file:
;
;   ;@axiom:pur above the template's FIRST declaration   -> nothing
;   ;@axiom:pur above the template's SECOND declaration  -> AX3039
;
; The zero was there so `expGiveTags` could park an INVOCATION's tags
; on the first generated `fn` unconditionally. It does not need to be:
; that walk already reads each generated declaration's own word 7 to
; decide whether it is spoken for, and `made[0]`'s copy was never
; zeroed - only the invocation node's was.
;
; Two arms, both of which must FIRE, because the defect's signature is
; silence:
;
;   `loud`   the first template declaration is a `::` carrying
;            `restrict(no-io)`, over a body that calls `println`
;            -> AX3049, with the path
;   `quiet`  the first template declaration is a `fn` carrying
;            `effect(io)`, over a body that performs nothing
;            -> AX3010, the claim the body does not support
;
; and one control that must stay SILENT:
;
;   `plain`  the same shape with no tag on the first declaration - so
;            a fix that handed some tag to every element 0 would be
;            caught here rather than shipped
(import IO)

(macro defLoud ((defLoud nm)
  ;@axiom:restrict(no-io)
  (:: nm (-> Int Int))
  ;@axiom:effect(io)
  (fn (nm n)
    {
      (println "io")
      n
    }
  )))

(macro defQuiet ((defQuiet nm)
  ;@axiom:effect(io)
  (fn (nm n) n)
  (:: nm (-> Int Int))))

(macro defPlain ((defPlain nm)
  (:: nm (-> Int Int))
  (fn (nm n) n)))

(defLoud loud)

(defQuiet quiet)

(defPlain plain)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  {
    (loud 1)
    (quiet 2)
    (plain 3)
  }
)
